# A DIAMOND EDB for the retract-raises-proof-height demonstration: the chain
# a -> b -> c PLUS a direct shortcut a -> c. Plain Turtle triples (default graph);
# the `gmeow logic session` loader re-homes them into the single session world.
#
# Over the `reach` transitive-closure program, `reach(a, c)` therefore has TWO
# independent proofs:
#   * direct:     reach(a,c) :- edge(a,c)                     → proof height 1
#   * transitive: reach(a,c) :- edge(a,b), reach(b,c)         → proof height 2
# so its maintained min-proof-height is 1. Retiring the direct a -> c edge (see
# `diamond-retract.ttl`) drops the height-1 proof; `reach(a,c)` survives only via the
# transitive path, so its min-proof-height RISES 1 -> 2.
@prefix ex: <https://example.org/session/> .

ex:a ex:edge ex:b .
ex:b ex:edge ex:c .
ex:a ex:edge ex:c .
